1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,120
Okay, next section, benign tumors and fibrocystic changes.

2
00:00:03,780 --> 00:00:05,920
We're going to start with fibrocystic change,

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,260
and in order to understand this,

4
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:08,820
I'm going to take you back to the whiteboard.

5
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:12,100
So let's remind ourselves that the functional unit of the breast

6
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:14,240
is called the terminal duct lobular unit,

7
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:16,100
so that you've got this terminal duct,

8
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:18,100
which feeds into something called the lobule,

9
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:21,080
and of course the lobule contains these small little glands

10
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:22,720
which produce milk.

11
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:24,860
So that's the terminal duct lobular unit.

12
00:00:25,220 --> 00:00:26,960
Now the idea in fibrocystic change

13
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:30,560
is that you get cystic change of these circles,

14
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:31,920
so that they become bigger.

15
00:00:32,040 --> 00:00:33,180
That's what we mean by cysts.

16
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:35,680
You can also get cystic change here of the terminal duct.

17
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:38,180
And at the same time, as you get those cysts,

18
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:40,160
that's going to stretch the connective tissue a little bit,

19
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:42,220
and so you're going to get a little bit of fibrosis

20
00:00:42,220 --> 00:00:43,520
in between the connective tissue,

21
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:46,180
and hence the term fibrocystic change.

22
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:51,200
Now this is the most common change in a premenopausal woman,

23
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:53,020
and of course I call it a change

24
00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:56,100
because we currently believe it to be hormone-mediated,

25
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:58,380
and it's basically a normal variation

26
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:00,520
that can occur within breast tissue

27
00:01:00,520 --> 00:01:03,100
as a consequence of the up and down levels

28
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:04,540
of estrogen and progesterone

29
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:06,440
that are, again, present within the blood.

30
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:08,620
So you've got this rising and changing levels

31
00:01:08,620 --> 00:01:10,680
of estrogen and progesterone over time

32
00:01:10,680 --> 00:01:12,560
that can result in fibrocystic change.

33
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:15,240
The classic presentation on physical exam

34
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:17,860
would be to have a vague irregularity

35
00:01:17,860 --> 00:01:18,900
to the breast tissue

36
00:01:18,900 --> 00:01:20,440
where you don't feel a definite mass,

37
00:01:20,540 --> 00:01:22,380
but it feels a little lumpy in places,

38
00:01:22,980 --> 00:01:25,020
and so they also call that the lumpy breast.

39
00:01:25,020 --> 00:01:27,300
Usually it's in the upper outer quadrant,

40
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:28,740
but that's nothing special

41
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:31,740
because we know that much of the breast parenchyma

42
00:01:31,740 --> 00:01:33,920
in a female is in the upper outer quadrant.

43
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:36,180
That's the highest density of breast tissue

44
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:37,980
in the female breast anatomically,

45
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:41,120
and when you look at the tissue on gross exam,

46
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:42,820
you can actually see the cysts,

47
00:01:42,820 --> 00:01:43,660
and when you see the cysts,

48
00:01:43,700 --> 00:01:45,320
they often have a blue color to them,

49
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:48,980
so we call them blue-dome cysts on gross exam.

50
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:51,040
All of this is stated in your text.

51
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:52,540
I'll just quickly run through it with you.

52
00:01:52,540 --> 00:01:54,860
Development of fibrosis in cysts,

53
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:57,200
most common change in premenopausal breast,

54
00:01:57,700 --> 00:02:00,040
lumpy breast, upper outer quadrant,

55
00:02:00,460 --> 00:02:02,960
and the cysts usually have a blue-domed appearance

56
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:04,000
on gross exam.

57
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:06,660
I've explained all of that using the whiteboard already.

58
00:02:07,180 --> 00:02:10,920
Now, important to note that fibrocystic change is benign.

59
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:15,100
Number one, inherently, in and of itself, it's benign,

60
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:18,700
and number two, it carries no increased risk for cancer.

61
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:22,580
So the classic fibrocystic change carries no increased risk for cancer.

62
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:26,380
However, sometimes when a patient has fibrocystic change

63
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:28,480
and you do a biopsy to confirm it,

64
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:30,200
you can find other features,

65
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:32,920
and some of those associated other features

66
00:02:32,920 --> 00:02:36,200
do carry a risk for cancer in the future.

67
00:02:36,860 --> 00:02:38,900
And so that's what I want to briefly mention here,

68
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,560
and this is particularly high yield,

69
00:02:40,620 --> 00:02:42,480
so I'm going to run through just the few ones

70
00:02:42,480 --> 00:02:44,360
that classically show up on examinations.

71
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:48,020
One possibility is that when a woman has fibrocystic change,

72
00:02:48,020 --> 00:02:50,860
and she's simply got fibrosis, and she's got cysts,

73
00:02:50,860 --> 00:02:54,560
and some of those cysts can be lined by apocrine metoplasia.

74
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:59,300
Now, important to note that when you have fibrosis, cysts,

75
00:02:59,300 --> 00:03:02,060
and apocrine metoplasia, or any one of these three,

76
00:03:02,420 --> 00:03:05,080
they are benign, and there's no increased risk

77
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:08,660
for future development of invasive carcinoma.

78
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:12,340
So that's the first set, fibrosis, cysts, and apocrine metoplasia.

79
00:03:12,580 --> 00:03:15,320
Now, this apocrine metoplasia is actually particularly high yield

80
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:17,920
because one of the general principles in pathology

81
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:19,640
is that any time you have metoplasia,

82
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:22,720
it's usually a risk factor for the future development of cancer.

83
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:28,080
For example, Barrett's esophagus is a non-ciliated columnar cell

84
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:29,840
with goblet cell metoplasia

85
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:33,060
that increases the risk for development of adenocarcinoma.

86
00:03:33,740 --> 00:03:36,780
For example, squamous metoplasia in the lung

87
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:38,780
increases the risk for dysplasia

88
00:03:38,780 --> 00:03:42,880
and the subsequent development of squamous cell carcinoma in smokers.

89
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:46,280
However, apocrine metoplasia, very high yield to note,

90
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:49,320
apocrine metoplasia does not increase the risk for cancer.

91
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:51,060
This is why I'm emphasizing it so much

92
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:53,280
because despite the fact that we call it a metaplasia,

93
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:55,560
there's no increased risk for cancer.

94
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:57,760
Okay, the second change that you could see

95
00:03:57,760 --> 00:03:59,640
is something called ductal hyperplasia,

96
00:04:00,060 --> 00:04:02,400
and the idea here is that you've got your duct, correct,

97
00:04:02,540 --> 00:04:05,320
that goes in, and it goes into the terminal duct lobular unit,

98
00:04:05,420 --> 00:04:06,440
so this would be the lobule.

99
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:10,160
And remember that the normal lining of the duct is two layers.

100
00:04:10,160 --> 00:04:13,860
You've got an epithelial layer, which is like a columnar cell,

101
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:16,360
and underneath that you've got a myoepithelial cell.

102
00:04:16,820 --> 00:04:18,760
Now, normally there should only be two cells

103
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:20,740
that line this entire surface.

104
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:22,580
However, you can have hyperplasia

105
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:24,500
where you get excess numbers of cells

106
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:26,160
and where you get excess numbers of cells

107
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:27,380
and those cells are benign.

108
00:04:27,700 --> 00:04:29,120
We call that ductal hyperplasia.

109
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:32,840
Now, ductal hyperplasia has a two times increased risk

110
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:34,140
of development of cancer,

111
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:37,120
so that if a normal woman has her standard risk,

112
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:40,460
she now, if she has ductal hyperplasia on a biopsy,

113
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:43,500
she now has a two times increased risk

114
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:47,480
of developing invasive carcinoma sometime in the future.

115
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,460
Another disorder that could result in an increased risk

116
00:04:51,460 --> 00:04:53,620
would be something called sclerosing adenosis.

117
00:04:54,260 --> 00:04:56,520
Examiners do ask about this, so I'm going to discuss it.

118
00:04:56,760 --> 00:04:59,920
The idea here is if you've got the normal terminal duct lobular unit,

119
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:03,280
remember that normally, let's say that in this normal unit,

120
00:05:03,380 --> 00:05:05,500
you should have had three or four glands.

121
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:08,660
Now, in adenosis, what happens is you have too many glands,

122
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:09,980
so instead of having three or four,

123
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:12,780
you have, I don't know, 10 or 15, for example.

124
00:05:12,900 --> 00:05:13,980
That would be adenosis.

125
00:05:14,580 --> 00:05:17,340
And then sometimes you can get some fibrosis

126
00:05:17,340 --> 00:05:18,920
associated with that adenosis,

127
00:05:19,060 --> 00:05:21,220
making this area quote-unquote hard

128
00:05:21,220 --> 00:05:23,360
or with deposition of collagen,

129
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:24,640
and that's called sclerosis.

130
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:27,560
And so sclerosing adenosis, where it to be present,

131
00:05:28,020 --> 00:05:30,780
increases the risk by twofold,

132
00:05:31,100 --> 00:05:34,120
so that the patients who have sclerosing adenosis on a biopsy

133
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:35,840
will have a two-times-increased risk

134
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:38,480
for the future development of invasive carcinoma.

135
00:05:38,900 --> 00:05:41,200
Now, very important to note, and high yield for examination,

136
00:05:41,740 --> 00:05:46,160
is that sclerosing adenosis is classically often calcified,

137
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:48,720
so that there can be calcifications

138
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:50,480
associated with sclerosing adenosis,

139
00:05:50,780 --> 00:05:52,820
and that may be why the biopsy occurs.

140
00:05:52,820 --> 00:05:55,840
A woman goes for a mammogram,

141
00:05:56,020 --> 00:05:57,460
there's increased calcifications,

142
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:58,740
and so a biopsy is performed,

143
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:01,140
and it actually turns out to be sclerosing adenosis.

144
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:04,940
Again, sclerosing adenosis is benign in and of itself,

145
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:07,960
but it pretends an increased risk for the development,

146
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:10,440
for the future development of breast cancer.

147
00:06:11,020 --> 00:06:13,640
And the third possibility that I've listed here

148
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:15,200
is atypical hyperplasia.

149
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:18,760
Now, it's possible when you look at the terminal duct

150
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:21,680
and the lobule, it's possible that you could have

151
00:06:21,680 --> 00:06:27,280
atypical cells that are increased within the duct,

152
00:06:27,940 --> 00:06:29,780
or you could have atypical cells

153
00:06:29,780 --> 00:06:31,860
that are increased within the lobule.

154
00:06:32,220 --> 00:06:33,060
When it's in the duct,

155
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:35,260
we call that atypical ductal hyperplasia.

156
00:06:35,620 --> 00:06:36,480
When it's in the lobule,

157
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:39,360
we call that atypical lobular hyperplasia.

158
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:41,620
Classically, I'm simplifying this a little bit,

159
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:43,080
but that's the classic understanding.

160
00:06:43,620 --> 00:06:44,820
But the point is that if you have

161
00:06:44,820 --> 00:06:47,620
any type of atypical hyperplasia on a biopsy,

162
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:50,360
the woman now has a five times increased risk

163
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:53,100
for the future development of invasive carcinoma.

164
00:06:54,120 --> 00:06:55,380
Now, I'd like to say one more thing

165
00:06:55,380 --> 00:06:56,660
that shows up on examinations,

166
00:06:57,080 --> 00:06:59,300
and that is that you have to know, first of all,

167
00:06:59,620 --> 00:07:02,220
that the increased risk is an increased risk

168
00:07:02,220 --> 00:07:04,800
for invasive carcinoma, all right?

169
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:05,460
That's important.

170
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:08,120
It's an increased risk for invasive carcinoma,

171
00:07:08,340 --> 00:07:11,700
and that that increased risk applies to both breasts,

172
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:15,280
so that the risk is for cancer in either breast.

173
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:18,660
So if the biopsy was performed on the right breast

174
00:07:18,660 --> 00:07:21,020
and they saw atypical hyperplasia on the right breast,

175
00:07:21,380 --> 00:07:24,180
the risk for cancer applies to both the right

176
00:07:24,180 --> 00:07:25,520
and the left breast,

177
00:07:25,620 --> 00:07:27,440
so that's important to understand as well.

178
00:07:27,960 --> 00:07:30,160
Here's a classic picture of apocrine metaplasia.

179
00:07:30,580 --> 00:07:32,360
All I'm trying to show you is that these cells

180
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:34,160
have abundant pink cytoplasm,

181
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:36,580
and they're slightly larger than the normal cells.

182
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,280
Again, most important take-home point

183
00:07:39,280 --> 00:07:42,040
is that for you to know that apocrine metaplasia

184
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:44,120
has no increased risk for breast cancer,

185
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:46,580
despite the fact that it's called metaplasia.

186
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:52,040
Now, introductal papilloma is the next type of disorder

187
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:54,160
that we want to discuss, and this is a benign tumor.

188
00:07:54,320 --> 00:07:55,380
Notice that it's an oma.

189
00:07:55,500 --> 00:07:56,400
It's a true mass.

190
00:07:57,020 --> 00:07:58,140
In introductal papilloma,

191
00:07:58,200 --> 00:07:59,420
the way you want to think about this

192
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:00,820
is to simply go back to normal.

193
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:03,380
Let's talk about the very large duct

194
00:08:03,380 --> 00:08:06,600
that goes out into the skin of the nipple.

195
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:08,360
Now, when you have a large duct

196
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:12,100
within the anterior portion of the breast,

197
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:14,380
one of the possibilities that can occur

198
00:08:14,380 --> 00:08:15,880
is that within this large duct,

199
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:17,460
which, of course, is normally lined

200
00:08:17,460 --> 00:08:18,940
with just two layers of cells,

201
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:21,760
you can develop a finger-like projection

202
00:08:21,760 --> 00:08:24,600
which is lined by epithelial cells.

203
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:25,480
All right?

204
00:08:25,540 --> 00:08:27,880
And, of course, a growth of a finger-like projection

205
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:31,640
lined by epithelial cells would be a papillary lesion,

206
00:08:31,880 --> 00:08:34,980
papillary because it has a finger-like projection

207
00:08:34,980 --> 00:08:37,920
with a fibrovascular core blood vessel

208
00:08:37,920 --> 00:08:39,000
running through the center.

209
00:08:39,760 --> 00:08:42,240
So that would be a papillary lesion,

210
00:08:42,320 --> 00:08:43,800
and when you have a papillary lesion,

211
00:08:43,880 --> 00:08:45,820
one of the key features of the papillary lesion

212
00:08:45,820 --> 00:08:47,740
is that it often bleeds,

213
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:51,020
producing a bloody nipple discharge.

214
00:08:51,640 --> 00:08:54,900
So the classic association with a papillary lesion

215
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:56,480
is a bloody nipple discharge.

216
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Now, for the most part,

217
00:08:58,160 --> 00:08:59,300
these papillary lesions,

218
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:01,980
especially in a premenopausal woman,

219
00:09:02,540 --> 00:09:04,820
are going to represent papilloma.

220
00:09:04,980 --> 00:09:07,020
Something called intraductal papilloma.

221
00:09:07,140 --> 00:09:08,560
Intraductal because it's in the duct

222
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:10,340
and papilloma because it's benign.

223
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:12,760
And one of the very important hallmarks

224
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:14,420
concerning the intraductal papilloma

225
00:09:14,420 --> 00:09:16,780
is that since this is a benign proliferation

226
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:17,620
of epithelium,

227
00:09:17,980 --> 00:09:19,660
you'll actually have two cell types

228
00:09:19,660 --> 00:09:21,520
lining this intraductal papilloma.

229
00:09:21,680 --> 00:09:23,920
You'll have your standard epithelial cell,

230
00:09:24,260 --> 00:09:25,060
and underneath that,

231
00:09:25,140 --> 00:09:26,720
you'll have a myoepithelial cell.

232
00:09:27,040 --> 00:09:28,660
So this is a very high yield,

233
00:09:28,760 --> 00:09:30,140
shows up in exams all the time,

234
00:09:30,260 --> 00:09:30,700
principle,

235
00:09:31,340 --> 00:09:33,560
that when you have an intraductal papilloma,

236
00:09:33,560 --> 00:09:35,740
there will be the standard two cell layers.

237
00:09:35,880 --> 00:09:37,300
There will be an epithelial cell,

238
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:39,540
underneath which is a myoepithelial cell.

239
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:41,880
Another important thing about intraductal papilloma,

240
00:09:41,980 --> 00:09:43,800
it usually occurs in a premenopausal woman.

241
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:46,580
Now, it is possible to develop a papillary growth

242
00:09:46,580 --> 00:09:47,620
just like this.

243
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:50,340
However, instead of it being an intraductal papilloma,

244
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:52,200
it's a papillary carcinoma.

245
00:09:52,620 --> 00:09:53,800
That's a possibility as well.

246
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:55,520
Now, how would you distinguish the two?

247
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:56,340
Well, number one,

248
00:09:56,480 --> 00:09:59,540
a papillary carcinoma is more common as women age,

249
00:09:59,540 --> 00:10:02,940
and it's more classically seen in a postmenopausal woman.

250
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:04,720
So, the older a woman gets,

251
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:07,540
the more likely she is to develop a papillary carcinoma

252
00:10:08,100 --> 00:10:09,940
as opposed to an intraductal papilloma.

253
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:10,600
That'd be one.

254
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:11,700
But more importantly,

255
00:10:11,860 --> 00:10:13,020
the key distinction is made

256
00:10:13,020 --> 00:10:15,700
by the lack of these myoepithelial cells,

257
00:10:15,860 --> 00:10:18,380
so that you wouldn't see these myoepithelial cells.

258
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:22,660
They would be absent in a papillary carcinoma,

259
00:10:22,860 --> 00:10:25,220
and that is classically very high yield

260
00:10:25,220 --> 00:10:26,620
for examination purposes.

261
00:10:26,620 --> 00:10:27,900
They love to go after this

262
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:29,180
because it's an opportunity

263
00:10:29,180 --> 00:10:31,360
to go after normal histology, in effect.

264
00:10:31,820 --> 00:10:33,220
So, that's the discussion of papilloma.

265
00:10:33,300 --> 00:10:34,180
Now, let's read together.

266
00:10:34,640 --> 00:10:34,980
So, I say,

267
00:10:35,060 --> 00:10:36,040
intraductal papilloma.

268
00:10:36,120 --> 00:10:37,420
This is a papillary growth,

269
00:10:37,740 --> 00:10:38,520
large duct.

270
00:10:38,900 --> 00:10:40,960
It has fibrovascular projections

271
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:42,480
lined by epithelial cells

272
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:44,140
and myoepithelial cells, right?

273
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:45,820
So, we're talking about the benign variant,

274
00:10:45,940 --> 00:10:47,140
the intraductal papilloma.

275
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:49,600
It's going to present with bloody nipple discharge

276
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:51,040
in a premenopausal woman,

277
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:53,880
but you must always have in the back of your mind

278
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:55,440
papillary carcinoma.

279
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:58,000
Again, the two features of papillary carcinoma

280
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,900
would be a lack of myoepithelial cells,

281
00:11:01,020 --> 00:11:02,960
so you wouldn't have that second layer

282
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:04,920
of myoepithelial cells, number one.

283
00:11:05,260 --> 00:11:05,960
And number two,

284
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:08,080
it's much more likely as women age,

285
00:11:08,140 --> 00:11:10,000
so that this would classically be a

286
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,720
postmenopausal female

287
00:11:11,720 --> 00:11:13,440
with bloody nipple discharge.

288
00:11:13,820 --> 00:11:15,040
And, of course, papillary lesions,

289
00:11:15,260 --> 00:11:17,060
the hallmark is bloody nipple discharge.

290
00:11:17,940 --> 00:11:19,440
The next disorder is called fibroadenoma.

291
00:11:20,160 --> 00:11:22,100
Fibro means fibrous tissue,

292
00:11:22,220 --> 00:11:23,280
and adeno means glands,

293
00:11:23,280 --> 00:11:24,920
and oma means you've got a true tumor.

294
00:11:25,420 --> 00:11:27,960
So, this is a tumor of fibrous tissue and glands.

295
00:11:28,460 --> 00:11:32,200
It is the most common benign tumor of the breast.

296
00:11:32,280 --> 00:11:34,060
Most common benign tumor of the breast.

297
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:37,680
Now, it's classically seen in a premenopausal woman.

298
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:40,120
In fact, you could say it's the most common tumor

299
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:42,260
in premenopausal females.

300
00:11:42,420 --> 00:11:43,200
I'm going to repeat that.

301
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:46,700
Most common tumor in premenopausal females.

302
00:11:46,700 --> 00:11:49,500
Now, this grows as a well-circumscribed,

303
00:11:49,880 --> 00:11:52,060
mobile, marble-like mass.

304
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:54,940
These are the classic descriptions of a benign tumor

305
00:11:54,940 --> 00:11:56,260
from our neoplasia chapter.

306
00:11:56,580 --> 00:11:58,660
Remember, I told you that when you have a benign tumor,

307
00:11:58,760 --> 00:12:01,140
it tends to be very distinct from the rest of the tissue,

308
00:12:01,380 --> 00:12:02,600
i.e., well-circumscribed.

309
00:12:02,980 --> 00:12:04,040
It tends to be mobile,

310
00:12:04,380 --> 00:12:06,760
indicating that it hasn't invaded into, for example,

311
00:12:06,840 --> 00:12:09,200
the chest wall or the rest of the breast tissue.

312
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:10,520
And it's marble-like,

313
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:12,860
and that's, again, indicating that it's clearly distinct

314
00:12:12,860 --> 00:12:13,960
from the rest of the breast.

315
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:16,420
And so these are some classic clinical features

316
00:12:16,420 --> 00:12:17,820
of a fibroadenoma.

317
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:19,720
These tumors are estrogen-sensitive,

318
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:20,520
and that's important.

319
00:12:20,660 --> 00:12:22,380
For example, they grow during pregnancy.

320
00:12:22,800 --> 00:12:24,740
They can be painful during the menstrual cycle.

321
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:26,980
They can shrink in size

322
00:12:26,980 --> 00:12:29,240
when a woman undergoes menopause.

323
00:12:29,740 --> 00:12:32,460
And so this is an important feature of fibroadenoma.

324
00:12:32,780 --> 00:12:34,640
And the most important, benign.

325
00:12:35,180 --> 00:12:36,860
But that's obvious because of the name.

326
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:37,800
It's an adenoma.

327
00:12:38,180 --> 00:12:40,100
It's not an adenocarcinoma, right?

328
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:41,360
And then number two,

329
00:12:41,640 --> 00:12:43,040
no increased risk for cancer.

330
00:12:43,040 --> 00:12:44,600
Once a woman has a fibroadenoma,

331
00:12:44,720 --> 00:12:45,480
she's going to ask you,

332
00:12:45,580 --> 00:12:46,820
so does this mean I have cancer?

333
00:12:47,020 --> 00:12:47,680
No, you don't.

334
00:12:47,920 --> 00:12:49,960
Does this mean I have an increased risk to get cancer?

335
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:51,300
No, you don't.

336
00:12:51,380 --> 00:12:54,500
So it is benign with no increased risk for carcinoma.

337
00:12:54,900 --> 00:12:56,620
Here's a classic picture of a fibroadenoma.

338
00:12:56,740 --> 00:12:57,640
What I'm trying to highlight here,

339
00:12:57,720 --> 00:12:58,540
this is the normal.

340
00:12:58,940 --> 00:12:59,820
This is the tumor.

341
00:13:00,140 --> 00:13:02,580
You can see that the tumor contains this fibrous tissue,

342
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:04,320
which, let's label this with F.

343
00:13:04,620 --> 00:13:07,640
And then you can see that it also contains these glands as well.

344
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:11,560
And so this is the combination of fibroadenoma,

345
00:13:11,560 --> 00:13:12,720
because it's a mass.

346
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:16,620
Now notice that this is sharply demarcated from the adjacent breast tissue.

347
00:13:17,020 --> 00:13:19,280
Again, it's a well-circumscribed, mobile-like,

348
00:13:19,620 --> 00:13:21,620
very distinct mass within the breast.

349
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:25,480
There is another type of fibroadenoma-like tumor

350
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:26,840
that can develop within the breast.

351
00:13:27,300 --> 00:13:28,700
It's called a phloides tumor.

352
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:30,820
It's very similar to the fibroadenoma

353
00:13:30,820 --> 00:13:33,080
in the sense that it has fibrous tissue and glands,

354
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:37,080
but there's an overgrowth of the fibrous component, high yield.

355
00:13:37,460 --> 00:13:39,860
There is an overgrowth of the fibrous component.

356
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:42,160
Now that overgrowth of the fibrous component

357
00:13:42,160 --> 00:13:46,440
then pushes out the tumor into these leaf-like projections.

358
00:13:47,140 --> 00:13:48,520
And this is what it looks like.

359
00:13:48,720 --> 00:13:51,760
So you've got this overgrowth of the fibrous component here.

360
00:13:51,880 --> 00:13:53,020
I'm labeling it with an F.

361
00:13:53,280 --> 00:13:54,560
And as you get the overgrowth,

362
00:13:54,680 --> 00:13:56,080
it pushes out the surface,

363
00:13:56,340 --> 00:13:58,200
creating these leaf-like projections.

364
00:13:58,200 --> 00:14:01,260
So I'm circling this leaf-like projection.

365
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:04,600
And that's the classic image of a phloides tumor.

366
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:06,640
Now I'd like to go back and remind you

367
00:14:06,640 --> 00:14:08,020
that when you have a fibroadenoma,

368
00:14:08,160 --> 00:14:09,800
that's usually a premenopausal woman.

369
00:14:10,140 --> 00:14:12,920
However, a phloides tumor is more commonly seen

370
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:14,580
in postmenopausal women,

371
00:14:14,700 --> 00:14:16,160
so women that are a little bit older

372
00:14:16,160 --> 00:14:19,780
than that of a fibroadenoma category.

373
00:14:20,380 --> 00:14:22,380
And another important thing about the phloides tumor

374
00:14:22,380 --> 00:14:23,720
is that it can be malignant.

375
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:25,540
But that would go along with the idea

376
00:14:25,540 --> 00:14:28,560
of it arising in postmenopausal women

377
00:14:28,560 --> 00:14:31,880
because we know that cancer is much more common

378
00:14:31,880 --> 00:14:33,420
in a postmenopausal woman.

379
00:14:33,560 --> 00:14:36,620
It's really classically a disease of postmenopausal women

380
00:14:36,620 --> 00:14:38,000
with one exception,

381
00:14:38,200 --> 00:14:39,720
and that would be genetic breast cancer,

382
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:41,500
which we're going to talk about at the very end.

383
00:14:42,160 --> 00:14:43,960
So again, that's the picture of fibroadenoma.

384
00:14:44,140 --> 00:14:48,040
And that closes off our discussion on the benign lesions.

385
00:14:48,180 --> 00:14:49,360
And then we're now going to enter

386
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:50,860
into a discussion of breast cancer.

